<?xpacket begin="ï»¿" id="W5M0MpCehiHzreSzNTczkc9d"?>
<x:xmpmeta xmlns:x="adobe:ns:meta/">
  <rdf:RDF xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#">
    <rdf:Description xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/" rdf:about="">
      <dc:title>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">The Inimitable Meowmeow</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:title>
      <dc:description>
        <rdf:Alt>
          <rdf:li xml:lang="x-default">&lt;p&gt;'For Greyskull's honour, Meowmeow! Who the devil are they?! The fellows staring at us, I mean.'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;'Those would be our potential readers, sir. They wish to assess our story. We must inform them that the tale updates regularly and content warnings are listed in the relevant chapter's notes. Volume 1 runs to Chapter 26; Volume 2 to 39; Volume 3 from 40. Mature chapters are flagged in their introduction, the rest are Teen and Up.'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;'Ah, yes! Readers. What Ho! Smashing to meet you - I'm Adora. Sir Adora de l'Horde, third Baronet, to be quite exact. And that other dashing madam? My gentlewoman's gentlewoman, Meowmeow. Oh... hang on. Old habits, old bean! I should rather say--- my girlfriend Catra. You're about to learn just quite how that came to be, from the very beginning. Plenty more thunders on around it too, what with my pal Bowregard, Her Ladyship Glimmer, and the whole cadre of lesbians we stumbled into. Oh, and the gender business. It all starts with the um... How do you say it, Meowmeow?'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;'Indictment for theft of a marine vehicle, sir.'&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;'No, no, not that. The um... The meet-cute! So strap on your buckled shoes, dust down your pinstripes, and away to the city streets of London in our year 1930.'&lt;/p&gt;</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Alt>
      </dc:description>
      <dc:creator>
        <rdf:Seq>
          <rdf:li>SleeveGartersSapphic</rdf:li>
        </rdf:Seq>
